s many files. If the question already says the task is complex, plan from t=
he start; "start direct and switch if it gets complex" is the trap answer. =
Plugins themselves aren't on the exam, and CLAUDE.md and rules always stay =
in the repo.</p></div>
      </section>

      <div class=3D"part">
        <p class=3D"kicker">Stretch =C2=B7 Step 15</p>
        <h2>For fast finishers</h2>
        <p>A bigger pile of text, and the habits that keep Claude accurate =
when its memory gets full.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 15 -->
      <section class=3D"step" id=3D"step-15" data-part=3D"4" data-title=3D"=
What customers love">
        <div class=3D"head">
          <div class=3D"stamp">15</div>
          <div>
            <div class=3D"meta"><span class=3D"obj">5.4</span></div>
            <h3>What customers love</h3>
            <p class=3D"learn">Keep track of findings across many files, ev=
en after Claude's memory is squeezed.</p>
          </div>
          <label class=3D"done"><input type=3D"checkbox" id=3D"done-15"> Do=
ne</label>
        </div>
        <p class=3D"plain"><b>In plain words:</b> when Claude's memory gets=
 squeezed, a notebook still has everything. So write in the notebook as you=
 go, not at the end.</p>
        <div class=3D"pb build">
          <div class=3D"pb-head"><span class=3D"tag">Build 1 of 3</span><sp=
an class=3D"where">Paste in Claude Code (in the Kettlebird studio)</span><b=
utton class=3D"copy" type=3D"button">Copy</button></div>
<pre class=3D"prompt">Create practice data: notes/reviews/ with 120 short m=
ade-up customer reviews of Kettlebird's earlier tea sampler box, in 6 files=
 of 20 reviews each (reviews-1.md to reviews-6.md). Make them varied and re=
alistic: name specific teas, mix praise with complaints (packaging, slow sh=
ipping, too little of a favourite tea, confusing brewing instructions), and=
 give each review a star rating. Don't summarise them.</pre>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"note"><b class=3D"lbl">Then</b><p>Start a named sessi=
on: <code>claude -n review-dig</code></p></div>
        <div class=3D"pb build">
          <div class=3D"pb-head"><span class=3D"tag">Build 2 of 3</span><sp=
an class=3D"where">Paste in the named session</span><button class=3D"copy" =
type=3D"button">Copy</button></div>
<pre class=3D"prompt">Find the top 5 things customers love and the top 3 co=
mplaints across all the reviews in notes/reviews/.

Use a subagent to read the review files, so the raw reviews don't fill up t=
his conversation. Tell the subagent to keep a scratchpad at notes/scratchpa=
d.md and to add to it after each file, one line per finding: the file, the =
finding, how many reviews mention it, and one short quote. At the end, give=
 me the top 5 and top 3 with how often each came up.</pre>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"note"><b class=3D"lbl">Then</b><p>Type <code>/compact=
</code>. This squeezes the conversation into a short summary.</p></div>
        <div class=3D"pb build">
          <div class=3D"pb-head"><span class=3D"tag">Build 3 of 3</span><sp=
an class=3D"where">Same session, after /compact</span><button class=3D"copy=
" type=3D"button">Copy</button></div>
<pre class=3D"prompt">Which review file had the most complaints about damag=
ed or wet packaging? Quote one. Answer from memory first. Then check notes/=
scratchpad.md and the files, and tell me whether your memory was right.</pr=
e>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"pb check">
          <div class=3D"pb-head"><span class=3D"tag">Check</span><span clas=
s=3D"where">New session, then paste</span><button class=3D"copy" type=3D"bu=
tton">Copy</button></div>
<pre class=3D"prompt">Check my scratchpad. Don't change any files.

1. Does notes/scratchpad.md have lines for every file in notes/reviews/?
2. Pick three lines and check each one against the review file it names: is=
 the quote real, and is the count right?

Give me a short table: Test | Pass or Fail | What you found.
Then ask me two quick questions, one at a time: why we write to a scratchpa=
d as we go, and what /compact does to Claude's memory.</pre>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"pair">
          <div class=3D"worked"><h4>You'll know it worked when</h4><ul>
            <li>Your main session only sends work to a subagent. The raw re=
views never fill your chat.</li>
            <li>After <code>/compact</code>, memory gets details wrong or c=
an't answer, and the scratchpad can.</li>
            <li>When we tried this with a thin scratchpad (one line per fil=
e), it couldn't answer either. Write one line per finding.</li>
          </ul></div>
          <div class=3D"exam"><h4>Exam note</h4><p>The warning sign is answ=
ers that stop matching earlier findings, or that talk about "typical patter=
ns" instead of the specific things found. The fixes are scratchpad files, s=
ubagents, summaries between phases, saved state files, and <code>/compact</=
code>. A bigger context window is never the answer.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class=3D"closing" id=3D"exam-map">
        <h2>Exam map</h2>
        <p style=3D"color:var(--muted);max-width:68ch">Where each CCAR-F Cl=
aude Code objective is practised in this course.</p>
        <div class=3D"tbl">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Objective</th><th>What it covers</th><th>Steps</=
th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class=3D"n">3.1</td><td>CLAUDE.md levels, @import, fo=
lder CLAUDE.md, /memory</td><td>2, 3, 5</td></tr>
              <tr><td class=3D"n">3.2</td><td>Commands and skills: argument=
-hint, context: fork, allowed-tools</td><td>4, 8</td></tr>
              <tr><td class=3D"n">3.3</td><td>Rules with paths: patterns</t=
d><td>6</td></tr>
              <tr><td class=3D"n">3.4</td><td>Plan mode, sending work to su=
bagents</td><td>14, 15</td></tr>
              <tr><td class=3D"n">3.5</td><td>Interview first, input/output=
 examples, fixes in one message</td><td>3, 5, 7</td></tr>
              <tr><td class=3D"n">3.6</td><td>Fresh-session review, -p, JSO=
N schema, re-review</td><td>7, 13</td></tr>
              <tr><td class=3D"n">1.7</td><td>Resume by name, fork, fresh s=
tart with a summary</td><td>12</td></tr>
              <tr><td class=3D"n">2.4</td><td>.mcp.json, ${VAR} credentials=
, use what exists first</td><td>1, 9</td></tr>
              <tr><td class=3D"n">2.5</td><td>Glob and Grep</td><td>7</td><=
/tr>
              <tr><td class=3D"n">1.5</td><td>Hooks: the exam names PostToo=
lUse; PreToolUse is what blocks</td><td>10, 14</td></tr>
              <tr><td class=3D"n">5.4</td><td>Big context: scratchpad, suba=
gents, /compact</td><td>15</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p style=3D"color:var(--muted);font-size:0.92rem">Not practised her=
e: MCP resources (catalogs of data), Edit's fallback when its anchor text i=
sn't unique (Read, then Write), and tracing code through a wrapper module.<=
/p>
      </section>

      <section class=3D"closing" id=3D"words">
        <h2>Words you'll see</h2>
        <div class=3D"words">
          <div class=3D"word"><b>Session</b><span>One conversation with Cla=
ude Code. <code>/exit</code> ends it; running <code>claude</code> starts a =
new one.</span></div>
          <div class=3D"word"><b>Commit</b><span>A saved snapshot of your f=
iles in git. You can always go back to it.</span></div>
          <div class=3D"word"><b>Plugin</b><span>A package of skills, comma=
nds, hooks and connections that you install in one go.</span></div>
          <div class=3D"word"><b>Skill</b><span>Saved instructions Claude f=
ollows when you call it with <code>/name</code>, or when the task fits.</sp=
an></div>
          <div class=3D"word"><b>MCP server</b><span>A connection that give=
s Claude tools from another service, like Resend.</span></div>
          <div class=3D"word"><b>Hook</b><span>A small script Claude Code r=
uns at a set moment, like just before a tool runs. It can block the action.=
</span></div>
          <div class=3D"word"><b>Practice mode</b><span>Resend's tools conn=
ected to a pretend email server on your own computer.</span></div>
          <div class=3D"word"><b>Fresh session</b><span>A new conversation =
that doesn't remember the old one, which makes it a fair checker.</span></d=
iv>
        </div>
      </section>

    </main>
  </div>
</div>



